{"relationshipsSections":[{"kind":"relationships","identifiers":["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/s16SendableMetatypeP"],"type":"conformsTo","title":"Conforms To"}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/umachallenger"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"UmaChallenger","kind":"identifier"}]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"anchor":"overview","type":"heading","text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Hand one to "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/AxiamGuards\/requireAccess(_:resource:scope:umaChallenge:)"},{"type":"text","text":" and a denial stops"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"being a bare 403: the guard mints a fresh permission ticket for the pair the caller lacked and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"attaches it to the thrown ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/AuthzError","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":", so the framework adapter can return it as a header and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"a UMA-aware client knows where to go for authority instead of only being told “no”.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Opt-in, and deliberately so."}]},{"text":" Emitting a challenge means minting a credential — a wire call","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"to the Protection API, and a live ticket, produced on a path the caller did not explicitly","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"request. A guard that did that on every denial by default would turn each unauthorized request","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"into a Protection API call, which is a denial-of-service amplifier pointed at your own","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"authorization server. So it happens only where an application asked for it."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Failure is not escalation."}]},{"type":"text","text":" If minting fails — the PAT expired, the Protection API is down,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the resource declares none of the requested scopes — the denial still surfaces as an ordinary"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/AuthzError"},{"type":"text","text":" without a challenge. A caller who was going to be refused is refused either way;"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"letting a Protection API outage turn a deny into a 503 would hand the outage a second"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"consequence, and letting it turn into an allow would be a security bug."}]}]}],"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"AxiamSDK"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"text":"UmaChallenger","kind":"identifier"}],"symbolKind":"struct","externalID":"s:8AxiamSDK13UmaChallengerV","title":"UmaChallenger","roleHeading":"Structure","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"UmaChallenger","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol"},"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A configured "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"WWW-Authenticate: UMA"},{"type":"text","text":" challenge emitter (CONTRACT.md §20.3, emit half)."}],"sections":[],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/UmaChallenger"},"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK"]]},"topicSections":[{"generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/UmaChallenger\/init(realm:asURI:pat:)"],"title":"Initializers","anchor":"Initializers"},{"generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/UmaChallenger\/asURI","doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/UmaChallenger\/pat","doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/UmaChallenger\/realm"],"title":"Instance Properties","anchor":"Instance-Properties"}],"references":{"doc://AxiamSDK/documentation/AxiamSDK/UmaChallenger/pat":{"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/umachallenger\/pat","identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/UmaChallenger\/pat","title":"pat","abstract":[{"text":"A Protection API Token: a ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"client-credentials"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" token carrying the ","type":"text"},{"code":"uma_protection","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" scope","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(§20.2 rule 1). A user token cannot stand in — a minted ticket is bound to the ","type":"text"},{"code":"client_id","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"that minted it.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"pat","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Sensitive","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:8AxiamSDK9SensitiveV"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"String","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}],"type":"topic"},"doc://AxiamSDK/documentation/AxiamSDK":{"url":"\/documentation\/axiamsdk","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK","role":"collection","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The official Swift SDK for AXIAM (Access eXtended Identity and Authorization Management)."}],"title":"AxiamSDK"},"doc://AxiamSDK/documentation/AxiamSDK/UmaChallenger/init(realm:asURI:pat:)":{"type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"init","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"realm",